nodes.bodyText:
Create a standard way to:

synthesize a zero tangent for a pytree to be passed to jax.jvp
syntehsize a zero cotangent for a pytree to be passed to f_vjp (the backward pass returned by jax.vjp).


This is related to #11208.
Currently, I synthesize zero tangents like so:
def zero_tangent_like(value: Array) -> RealArray:
    if jnp.issubdtype(value.dtype, jnp.inexact):
        return np.zeros_like(value)
    return np.zeros_like(value, dtype=float0)
But this won't work with the new Jax random keys.  I would prefer a function that works with any pytree and produces a zero tangent for it.  It is also extremely weird that I have to return a Numpy array for a function that works exclusively with Jax.
Lots of discussion in another issue starting here: #14046 (comment).
It would be really useful for this to work with components of pytrees.  See #14046 (comment).
From a type annotation standpoint, would it make sense if the symbolic zero created for a Jax array also responded true to isinstance(x, jax.Array)?
